  {
    "name": "xxh32",
    "categories": [
      "xxHash"
    ],
    "description": "32-bit xxHash (XXH32) — the classic 32-bit member of the xxHash family. Fast and well-distributed; use when 32 bits is enough — for in-memory hashtables, lightweight checksums, or short-lived bucket assignment.\n\nAccepts an optional `UINTEGER` seed. Prefer `xxh3_64` when you don't have a specific reason to use the 32-bit format — XXH3 is faster on modern hardware and offers more headroom against collisions.",
    "examples": [
      {
        "description": "Hash a string",
        "code": "SELECT xxh32('hello world');",
