  {
    "name": "xxh3_128",
    "categories": [
      "xxHash"
    ],
    "description": "128-bit xxHash3 (XXH3_128) returned as a `UHUGEINT`. The wider hash space dramatically reduces accidental-collision probability for very large keyspaces (billions of distinct keys).\n\nUse when 64 bits feels tight — content fingerprints, dedup keys at scale, or any place a 64-bit birthday-bound starts to matter. For a portable hex digest instead of a number, use `xxh3_128_hex`.",
