  {
    "name": "xxh3_128_hex",
    "categories": [
      "xxHash"
    ],
    "description": "128-bit xxHash3 returned as a 32-character lowercase hex string in canonical xxHash byte order (`low64 || high64`), as defined by the xxHash specification.\n\nMatches the digest produced by `XXH128_canonicalFromHash` in C, `xxhash.xxh3_128().hexdigest()` in Python, and `xxhash-rust` when formatted as hex. Use it when the hash needs to be a string — Redis keys, filenames, or a fingerprint shared with non-SQL code.",
    "examples": [
      {
        "description": "32-char hex digest",
