  {
    "name": "rapidhash",
    "categories": [
      "RapidHash"
    ],
    "description": "RapidHash — a 64-bit non-cryptographic hash designed for exceptional speed while keeping competitive distribution quality. Frequently the fastest 64-bit hash in published benchmarks on modern x86_64.\n\nReach for `rapidhash` when `xxh3_64`'s throughput isn't quite enough, or when most of your hashed inputs are very short integers and you want the lowest per-call latency. As with the rest of this extension, this is **not** cryptographically secure — use `crypto` for digests and signatures.",
    "examples": [
      {
        "description": "Default",
        "code": "SELECT rapidhash('hello world');",
        "outputTable": {
          "columns": [
